# component: marker
# decisions: A11Y-2, API-16, DOC-1, DOC-2
# hunks:
#   A11Y-2: `markerVariants`' base string gains, scoped to `[a,button]:`, an invisible
#     `::after` hit area (`after:absolute after:inset-x-0 after:-inset-y-1 after:content-['']`).
#     Upstream's own "Links and Buttons" section renders the marker ROOT as an `<a>` or a
#     `<button>` through `render`; the row is then one line of 14px text over `min-h-4`, which
#     the geometry lane measures at 20px — 4px under SC 2.5.8 — and a marker row is a control
#     rather than prose, so the inline-text exception does not reach it. The area grows the
#     BLOCK axis only, so two stacked markers never fight for a pixel, and it is scoped to the
#     interactive spellings only, so a presentational marker is byte-identical to upstream.
#     `::after` with no background paints nothing. `marker.test.tsx` measures both shapes.
#   Nothing else. Upstream's marker paints no focus glow, sets no cursor, disables nothing and
#     opens no portal; `MarkerIcon` is already `aria-hidden`.
#   API-16: `"use client"` is ADDED. Upstream ships none, and this file calls
#     `useRender` from `@base-ui/react/use-render`, which calls `React.useRef` internally —
#     under the `react-server` condition that hook is `undefined`, so a server component
#     rendering it throws on import. `tooling/verify-rsc-safety.mjs` is what found it, the
#     same way it found `breadcrumb` in Batch 5. API-16 puts the boundary at the lowest
#     interactive leaf, and this file is it.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
